            "storyId": "session-lifecycle-api",
            "before": {
              "verdict": "partial",
              "quality": 4,
              "confidence": "medium",
              "rationale": "Mesh's own screening workflow can be driven through a documented API. You create and screen a customer synchronously or asynchronously, learn completion through a WORKFLOW_COMPLETED webhook, read the screening_result, and review or remediate cases via the API. A Postman collection and an OpenAPI 3.0.3 schema document these steps. This is AML screening rather than an identity-verification session, so captured media and cancel/redact steps have no evidence. missing for 10: verification-session create/status endpoints, retrieval of captured media (documents/selfies), cancel or redact endpoints, hands-on corroboration of the end-to-end lifecycle",
              "evidenceIds": [
                "complyadvantage-docs-11",
                "complyadvantage-docs-12",
                "complyadvantage-docs-13",
                "complyadvantage-docs-14",
                "complyadvantage-docs-10",
                "complyadvantage-scope-openapi-retrieval",
                "complyadvantage-scope-external-identifier-lookup"
              ],
              "productId": "complyadvantage",
              "storyId": "session-lifecycle-api"
            },
            "after": {
              "verdict": "none",
              "quality": 0,
              "confidence": "medium",
              "rationale": "ComplyAdvantage's documented API covers sanctions/PEP/adverse-media screening of customer records, cases, alerts, exports and audit trails. The evidence shows no identity-verification session that can be created, polled for status, have captured media retrieved, or be cancelled or redacted. Customer screening is an adjacent capability and earns no credit toward this verification-session lifecycle story.",
              "evidenceIds": [],
              "productId": "complyadvantage",
              "storyId": "session-lifecycle-api"
            },
            "feedback": "Customer screening records and their CRUD lifecycle are related to identity checks, but do not establish identity-verification sessions, captured-media handling, or cancel/redact steps. Apply the existing partial-credit boundary to the story itself. Credit only documented delivery of its requested capability.",
            "method": "Same judge, evidence, model and rubric with feature-boundary review feedback; no requested tier or quality."
          },
          {
            "storyId": "automation-rules-engine",
            "before": {
              "verdict": "partial",
              "quality": 4,
              "confidence": "low",
              "rationale": "ComplyAdvantage's own platform takes some automatic actions on events. Its agentic workflows auto-escalate high-risk cases and auto-remediate level 1 alerts, and users can set the risk-score equation, screening configurations and per-customer monitoring configurations that govern how alerts are raised. WORKFLOW_COMPLETED webhooks let downstream systems react to screening events. However, no evidence shows a general user-authored rules engine (if-event-then-action), and agent configurations cannot be customized on the Starter plan. Missing for 10: documented user-defined event→action rule authoring, configurable automated actions beyond alert/case handling, transaction-monitoring rule customization details, and independent or hands-on corroboration.",
              "evidenceIds": [
                "complyadvantage-docs-2",
                "complyadvantage-docs-5",
                "complyadvantage-docs-13",
                "complyadvantage-scope-monitor-config",
                "complyadvantage-scope-ai-escalation",
